{"title":"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/8824c3639f0d5ef50ae79cf637a0067af91fd8ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((3,-13)--(21.5,-5)--(19,-18)--(9,-18)--(10,-6)--(23,-14.5)--cycle); label(&quot;A&quot;,(3,-13),W);label(&quot;C&quot;,(21.5,-5),N);label(&quot;E&quot;,(19,-18),E);label(&quot;F&quot;,(9,-18),W);label(&quot;B&quot;,(10,-6),N);label(&quot;D&quot;,(23,-14.5),E); //Credit to Zimbalono for the diagram[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"165\" />\n</p><p>If the sum of the measures in degrees of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d3aceb48c0b97b786d49aff1b82fb6a5d5560f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,~B,~C,~D,~E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the figure above is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620b585f204d26aa21728b27bbb7d9b9f62896cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90n$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa352f7570dc8d869245e1ca4ca7ee68446d4452.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }2\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }3\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }4\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }5\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87fb4607141ba7f24ba18ac4c821b669d2d644b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APD = \\angle BPC$\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" /> are vertical angles, the angle sums of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a2ea219c5c2243456614ba0ea354a37e6fae35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458bae4d809ef768d59b1cb4ea8d8f895bc4149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PBC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> give:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3df1d84162870fd953e6385018ae915116ea7b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle A + \\angle D = 180^\\circ - \\angle APD\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae994edaabaff7dc1dcba4f37d7ea20235d70bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle B + \\angle C = 180^\\circ - \\angle BPC\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Adding these equations yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24fb61f96bfdc977186edde83b0577ed1ad0700f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle C + \\angle D = 360^\\circ - 2\\angle BPC\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Consider quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2dc9710551c04b6d7cfd2f73525e7927a9f82e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PFE C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. Its interior angle sum gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c5e0c2205508ee09ff7a5c3e6415a7dcc23ce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle E + \\angle F + \\angle BPC + \\text{adj angles} = 360^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"311\" height=\"18\" />, which simplifies the total sum of all six angles to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578284b66cd78f2e257fa2f1d8a2fa665b853d0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle C + \\angle D + \\angle E + \\angle F = 360^\\circ\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We are given that the sum equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999606c4fcff23b151784e969842f0190d7491bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90n^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc351251f1b99b4fc933d2015f862d59100d9934.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[90n = 360 \\implies n = 4\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b32acfcdd2f4bb76f3034350dd1e67726655d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME\" title=\"1972 AHSME\">1972 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1972 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1972 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1972\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl